      "This 'we' connects naturally to the apostolic community at Ephesus that stands behind the gospel. As we have already seen, Irenaeus locates John at Ephesus within a living community of apostolic testimony. The 'we' of 1:14 is not evidence of committee authorship or community composition — it is the voice of an eyewitness speaking from within and on behalf of the apostolic circle that shared his experience and vouches for his testimony. This reading is confirmed by the editorial note of 21:24 — 'we know that his testimony is true' — which we will examine in detail in section 3.5. The same apostolic 'we' that opens the gospel closes it.",
